    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Danza Contemporánea de Cuba  | Cuba, Here and Now | Feb 18 - 19, 2027 | Southam Hall"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#image": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "https://naccnaca-eventimages.s3.amazonaws.com/40362/9n1a1976-mejorado-nr__large.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-ca",
        "@value": "Turn Up the Heat\n\nDanza Contemporánea de Cuba is internationally recognized for its electrifying repertoire, and its high-powered dancers that bring it to life. This evening’s program beautifully epitomizes the company’s range and versatility.\n\nAnnabelle López Ochoa’s sensual Reversible is a battle of the sexes that plays with gender fluidity; dancers strut and tease, positioning strength and vulnerability in equal measure. Drawing on distinctly Cuban movements, Ochoa creates joyous, fearless physicality that will leave you wanting more.\n\nCuban choreographer George Céspedes is acclaimed for..."
      }
    ],
